      "author": "David Lafreniere",
      "maintainer": "David Lafreniere <endurodave.dev@gmail.com>",
      "sentence": "std::allocator for C++ standard library containers that uses fixed blocks (xallocator) instead of the heap.",
      "paragraph": "stl_allocator is a drop-in allocator for std::list, std::map, std::set, std::string, std::stringstream and more, with ready-made aliases (xlist, xmap, xset, xstring, xsstream, xqueue) and xmake_shared. Memory comes from xallocator's fixed blocks, so containers don't fragment the heap. Header only. Needs the C++ standard library (not 8-bit AVR).",
      "category": "Data Processing",
      "architectures": [
        "*"
      ],
      "depends": [
        "xallocator",
        "Allocator"
      ],
      "download_url": "https://downloads.arduino.cc/libraries/github.com/endurodave/stl_allocator-1.2.0.zip",
