      "author": "David Lafreniere",
      "maintainer": "David Lafreniere <endurodave.dev@gmail.com>",
      "sentence": "Fixed block replacement for malloc/free and new/delete in C++: no heap fragmentation, constant-time allocation.",
      "paragraph": "xmalloc, xfree, xrealloc and xcalloc hand out power-of-two blocks kept for reuse, and the XALLOCATOR macro routes a class's new/delete to them. Thread-safe with std::mutex or, through build options, FreeRTOS, ThreadX, Zephyr and CMSIS-RTOS2 locks. Built on the Allocator library. Needs the C++ standard library (not 8-bit AVR).",
      "category": "Data Processing",
      "architectures": [
        "*"
      ],
      "depends": [
        "Allocator"
      ],
      "download_url": "https://downloads.arduino.cc/libraries/github.com/endurodave/xallocator-1.3.0.zip",
